--[[
    THE RAKE: REMASTERED - Obsidian port of the Desire.cc menu

    Straight conversion of the Rayfield build: same features, same tabs, on
    the Obsidian library instead. Everything the old script knew is kept
    verbatim, because it is real ground truth learned off the running game -
    remote names, argument shapes, config keys, teleport coordinates.

    THREE THINGS WERE FIXED ON THE WAY ACROSS, and they are all the same bug:

      * The Rayfield build called RunService.Heartbeat:Connect INSIDE a
        Heartbeat handler, once per ESP object, and never disconnected any of
        them. Every scrap pile, every player, every supply crate added a
        permanent connection, and the ones belonging to objects that no
        longer exist kept running forever. That only ever gets worse. All the
        drawing now happens in ONE render loop.
      * Several toggles ran `repeat wait() until _G.Flag == false`, which
        spins a thread for as long as the feature is on. Toggles here only
        set a flag.
      * Drawing objects were never cleaned up, so unloading left them on
        screen. Everything created is tracked and destroyed on unload.

    RightShift opens the menu. Obsidian is fetched at runtime.
]]

